Z||000000||fierosound||03-07-2001||09:59 PM||||I'm looking at getting my driver's seat repaired by a local auto unholstery shop.  It's the usual thing, wear on the bolster on the driver's side.  The problem is, it seems unholstery fabric to match the original 1987 grey OEM fabric is no longer available, at least not through his regular suppliers.  Anyone know of a DEFINITE alternate supplier for matching automotive fabrics??  Thanks in advance...||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||03-07-2001||11:56 PM||||The Fiero Store has the original seat skins that they purchased from GM. Problem is you can only buy them in sets (read $$$$$) and since they are the OEM's they don't give the 10% discount  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Your best bet would be to find an excellent passenger seat and swap the seat back skins.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierosound||03-08-2001||12:33 AM||||I agree, but it's hard enough to find any kind of wrecked Fiero here, never mind good seats from GT.  I think the best bet may be finding someone who has redone their seats with Mr. Mike's leathers, and has ket their original covers.  <P>Anyone got a good original seatback skin for grey interior 1987 GT??||||reg||10
Z||000003||Hartz||03-08-2001||12:45 AM||||You might want to check with a local automotive/marine upholstry shop, but there are fabrics from the mid-80's Grand Ams that are nearly identical to the Fiero fabric, and much easier (cheaper) to get.  It's just a small shade of grey off.  Since I was redoing both of my seats, it was a no brainer.<P>Best of luck,<BR>Hartz<P>85 SE V6 Turbo||||reg||10
